1
00:02:13,870 --> 00:02:18,870
"The Demons that Lurk in the Moonlight"

2
00:03:11,250 --> 00:03:14,000
Coming straight at me--
is that all you can do?

3
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,080
If that's the case...

4
00:03:16,450 --> 00:03:19,910
You'll never become
a full-fledged knight, Kasel.

5
00:03:19,910 --> 00:03:23,120
What I'm trying to become
isn't a "full-fledged" knight!

6
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:25,410
I'm going to become a knight
that can protect everyone!

7
00:03:25,410 --> 00:03:26,580
There he goes again.

8
00:03:26,580 --> 00:03:28,620
Always with the big mouth!

9
00:03:28,620 --> 00:03:31,330
Then you should at least be able to beat me!

10
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,040
You're too straightforward, Kasel.

11
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:41,870
That could cost you dearly.

12
00:03:43,450 --> 00:03:44,660
Dammit!

13
00:03:47,950 --> 00:03:49,870
You've still got a long way to go
before you can beat me.

14
00:03:49,870 --> 00:03:52,500
I'm always one level above you.

15
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:54,700
You're just taller, that's it!

16
00:03:55,950 --> 00:03:59,700
I'm going to jump over that...

17
00:04:01,370 --> 00:04:02,580
...easily!

18
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:13,660
All right, time for work, Mr. Apprentice.

19
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:18,450
Gran, Flegg, you too--get to work.

20
00:04:18,450 --> 00:04:20,830
I know.

21
00:04:20,830 --> 00:04:23,910
Dang, so Clause wins again.

22
00:04:23,910 --> 00:04:26,620
It won't be easy, obviously.

23
00:04:26,620 --> 00:04:29,950
You owe me lunch, Flegg.

24
00:04:29,950 --> 00:04:36,330
Come on, Kasel. You need be strong enough
to protect my lunch, at least.

25
00:04:36,330 --> 00:04:38,330
That's not my concern.

26
00:04:38,330 --> 00:04:41,450
You're honest and a hard worker,
we'll give you that.

27
00:04:41,450 --> 00:04:42,370
Huh.

28
00:04:42,370 --> 00:04:46,330
You just need to work on
your stamina and your technique.

29
00:04:47,410 --> 00:04:51,080
I mean, you're not bad,
as far as apprentices go.

30
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:56,040
With Clause training you every day,
I'm sure you'll get stronger soon.

31
00:04:56,040 --> 00:05:00,540
Okay, and thus, lunch is on you, Kasel.

32
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:04,000
How does that follow?!
You're just making stuff up!

33
00:05:08,410 --> 00:05:10,330
So boring, as always.

34
00:05:10,330 --> 00:05:13,950
Are you sure you want to be
saying that while on patrol?

35
00:05:13,950 --> 00:05:18,410
It's fine. If we're bored,
that means it's peaceful.

36
00:05:18,410 --> 00:05:20,910
Oh, how joyful it is to be bored!

37
00:05:20,910 --> 00:05:23,700
But you don't have to announce it so loudly...

38
00:05:23,700 --> 00:05:29,450
Oh, I know. I have to stop by May's place
to make sure nothing dangerous happened!

39
00:05:29,450 --> 00:05:30,950
Hey, is that...

40
00:05:34,290 --> 00:05:35,790
A dark elf.

41
00:05:35,790 --> 00:05:38,290
What's a dark elf doing in Orvelia...?

42
00:05:51,700 --> 00:05:53,950
That's unsettling.

43
00:05:53,950 --> 00:05:56,540
Yes, what does he want?

44
00:05:56,540 --> 00:06:01,080
You're Guardian Knights, aren't you?
Why won't you throw him out?

45
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:05,000
Huh? But he hasn't done anything wrong...

46
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:09,120
It's a dark elf! Obviously he's up to no good!

47
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:13,080
Yeah, they're like
the embodiment of bad omens.

48
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:22,790
Please, folks, stay calm. I'll make sure
my superiors know about this.

49
00:06:22,790 --> 00:06:25,870
It's break time, right?
You go ahead and return.

50
00:06:25,870 --> 00:06:27,200
Yes...

51
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:31,620
Don't you worry now. The Guardian Knights
will maintain the peace in this town.

52
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:37,750
That looks delicious.

53
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:41,330
Yeah, it's very fresh.

54
00:06:41,330 --> 00:06:45,370
For a pretty priestess like you,
I'll toss in another one for free.

55
00:06:45,370 --> 00:06:47,410
Oh? Are you sure?

56
00:06:47,410 --> 00:06:49,040
Sure! Take it.

57
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:53,330
Thank you very much.
May the holy light protect you.

58
00:06:53,330 --> 00:06:54,370
Frey.

59
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:58,450
Kasel.

60
00:06:59,790 --> 00:07:02,160
I'm so glad I ran into you.

61
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:06,450
I haven't seen you in a while.
I was wondering how you were doing.

62
00:07:08,290 --> 00:07:13,750
Don't worry about me.
I'm doing fine, and Clause is with me.

63
00:07:13,750 --> 00:07:16,330
That's good to hear.

64
00:07:16,330 --> 00:07:22,200
I was worried that you'd eat something
strange again and upset your stomach.

65
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:24,870
When have I ever eaten
anything out of the ordinary?

66
00:07:24,870 --> 00:07:27,660
You always do. Like centipedes, spiders...

67
00:07:27,660 --> 00:07:29,660
There's nothing weird about that.

68
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:31,290
It is weird.

69
00:07:32,790 --> 00:07:38,620
Remember when we were small, you, me,
and Clause went insect hunting until sundown?

70
00:07:38,620 --> 00:07:43,080
Yeah, we lost track of time and
got dragged back to the orphanage.

71
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:47,750
The priest was so mad,
both Clause and I cried.

72
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:50,620
But you just fell asleep, exhausted.

73
00:07:50,620 --> 00:07:51,910
Really?

74
00:07:51,910 --> 00:07:56,580
Yes. Clause was surprised
that you had such nerves of steel.

75
00:08:01,250 --> 00:08:04,250
Kasel, you're working very hard as a knight.

76
00:08:04,250 --> 00:08:07,620
I'm still stuck at the apprentice level, though.

77
00:08:10,290 --> 00:08:12,250
Earlier today...

78
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:19,790
Well... A little incident happened in town,
but I couldn't stop it.

79
00:08:19,790 --> 00:08:21,040
I see.

80
00:08:22,160 --> 00:08:27,080
Well, you should finish
your apprenticeship soon, and look sharp.

81
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:29,910
I just want to be a knight
that can protect everyone.

82
00:08:29,910 --> 00:08:33,080
Nothing else matters.

83
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:35,330
You really don't change, do you?

84
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:44,120
Please enter.

85
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:52,040
My king, I have news.

86
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:55,200
Behl. What is it?

87
00:08:55,200 --> 00:09:00,120
We have received word of
Demon sightings in the King's Forest.

88
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:01,580
Demons...!

89
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:05,250
We will send out scouts immediately.

90
00:09:05,250 --> 00:09:09,040
We must not allow
a single Demon to enter Orvelia.

91
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:11,370
Yes, I understand.

92
00:09:11,370 --> 00:09:15,410
We are not where we were
100 years ago... If they do...

93
00:09:17,950 --> 00:09:19,870
I'm counting on you.

94
00:09:19,870 --> 00:09:21,040
Yes.

95
00:09:26,950 --> 00:09:28,870
Lord Moriham.

96
00:09:28,870 --> 00:09:30,250
This person...

97
00:09:30,250 --> 00:09:33,000
He is with me. Let us through.

98
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,500
That's a dark elf.

99
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:35,500
Yeah...

100
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:37,370
What are you waiting for?

101
00:09:37,370 --> 00:09:38,620
Y-Yes, sir!

102
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:42,950
B-But you'll need to hand in your weapon.

103
00:09:42,950 --> 00:09:44,290
Naturally.

104
00:09:45,660 --> 00:09:48,540
Demons in the King's Forest...

105
00:09:48,540 --> 00:09:51,450
Could the Dark Lord's armies be in Orvelia...?

106
00:09:51,450 --> 00:09:54,250
King Kyle destroyed the Dark Lord
a hundred years ago,

107
00:09:54,250 --> 00:09:56,910
in the Battle of Galluah Plains.

108
00:09:56,910 --> 00:09:59,160
That's impossible.

109
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:01,660
Even if it's not the actual Dark Legion,

110
00:10:01,660 --> 00:10:05,500
we still aren't sure
how many Demons there are.

111
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:09,910
We have no idea how many men
we would need to investigate this.

112
00:10:09,910 --> 00:10:12,750
Shouldn't we limit the sacrifice to a minimum?

113
00:10:12,750 --> 00:10:16,500
The size of the force to send
should be as small as possible.

114
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:20,750
If none return to give a report,
that would be completely useless!

115
00:10:20,750 --> 00:10:23,410
Greetings, everyone.

116
00:10:23,410 --> 00:10:25,080
Lord Moriham.

117
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:26,580
Who is this?

118
00:10:26,580 --> 00:10:30,040
He is my soldier, Chancellor.

119
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:32,500
But he's a dark elf...!

120
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:37,950
Why would you let someone like that
into the castle, Lord Moriham?!

121
00:10:37,950 --> 00:10:43,370
There is no law barring dark elves
from entering the castle.

122
00:10:43,370 --> 00:10:45,160
Or...

123
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:50,950
Did someone commit the unspeakable act
of making rules without the king's consent?

124
00:10:51,750 --> 00:10:54,950
So why did you bring him here?

125
00:10:54,950 --> 00:10:57,750
I have heard that we must
send scouts to investigate this.

126
00:10:57,750 --> 00:11:02,790
These men, the Black Edge,
should be useful to us.

127
00:11:02,790 --> 00:11:04,870
Black Edge...?

128
00:11:04,870 --> 00:11:08,870
A band of fierce mercenaries,
who are growing in fame.

129
00:11:08,870 --> 00:11:15,040
This man, Riheet, the leader of the Black Edge,
can take on 100 men alone.

130
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:16,160
--What?!
--What...?

131
00:11:17,540 --> 00:11:22,160
I ask you. The animosity between Orvelia
and the dark elves runs deep.

132
00:11:22,160 --> 00:11:25,830
What made you think of lending us aid?

133
00:11:25,830 --> 00:11:31,370
We are men for hire.
I have no interest in who hires me.

134
00:11:31,370 --> 00:11:35,450
I see... And what do you ask,
in return for your aid?

135
00:11:35,450 --> 00:11:39,450
Nothing... Pay us our rewards,
and I ask for nothing else.

136
00:11:39,450 --> 00:11:44,200
They are simple and clear.
That's what makes them trustworthy.

137
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:47,750
They are quite unlike those who, for example,
claim to work for the nation,

138
00:11:47,750 --> 00:11:51,290
yet concentrate on their own
political or financial gains.

139
00:11:53,330 --> 00:11:58,080
Chancellor, please,
make use of the Black Edge.

140
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:02,200
We cannot allow these suspicious strangers
to take on such an important mission...

141
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:06,370
There is no place in the defense
of Orvelia for these dark elves!

142
00:12:06,370 --> 00:12:08,160
I also oppose!

143
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:12,950
They are all correct.
We will be the ones to defend our nation.

144
00:12:14,830 --> 00:12:20,750
As you wish. My apologies
for speaking out of line.

145
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:32,870
How can you eat that thing?

146
00:12:32,870 --> 00:12:35,410
I'm getting heartburn just from watching...

147
00:12:35,410 --> 00:12:38,040
Whole-cooked spider is quite delicious.

148
00:12:39,330 --> 00:12:42,450
Kasel eats anything and eats a lot of it.

149
00:12:42,450 --> 00:12:44,700
If nothing else, his stomach is strong.

150
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:46,660
Yeah, sure...

151
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:49,250
By the way, I saw Frey earlier.

152
00:12:49,250 --> 00:12:50,250
Frey?

153
00:12:50,250 --> 00:12:55,540
Yeah, bumped into her in the street.
She's gotten very priestly.

154
00:12:57,540 --> 00:13:00,870
I see... Good to hear she's working hard.

155
00:13:00,870 --> 00:13:01,790
Yeah.

156
00:13:01,790 --> 00:13:05,580
Clause is a knight; Frey is a priestess.

157
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:07,910
You've both made your dreams come true.

158
00:13:07,910 --> 00:13:12,200
Kasel, you'll finish
your apprenticeship in no time, too.

159
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:15,000
Well, you always say I still
have a long way to go...

160
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:18,120
I'm changing my educational style.
From now on, it's positive reinforcement.

161
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:20,250
You should be thankful, Kasel.

162
00:13:20,250 --> 00:13:23,870
Yeah, Clause's training style is a bit harsh.

163
00:13:23,870 --> 00:13:25,950
What an understatement.

164
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:31,540
Kasel. I'm going off on a new mission.

165
00:13:31,540 --> 00:13:33,750
You won't be training with me for a while.

166
00:13:33,750 --> 00:13:34,790
Huh?

167
00:13:34,790 --> 00:13:38,370
We got word that Demons
were spotted in the King's Forest.

168
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:47,080
Our squad is being sent to investigate.
Gran and Flegg are going, too.

169
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:51,000
Make sure to keep training
while we're gone, all right?

170
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:54,200
Do spiders sound good for your souvenir?

171
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:55,500
Yes...

172
00:13:55,500 --> 00:14:01,370
Don't look so glum, Kasel.
This is what we knights are for.

173
00:14:01,370 --> 00:14:02,290
Yeah...

174
00:14:02,290 --> 00:14:06,120
Come on, eat up. You're buying tonight!

175
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,950
Again, why me...?

176
00:14:09,250 --> 00:14:11,370
H-Help me!

177
00:14:30,540 --> 00:14:32,660
Sneaking in here was easy!

178
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:35,450
That went well.

179
00:14:35,450 --> 00:14:40,580
Yeah. You had no trouble
getting inside that castle, Riheet.

180
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:42,370
Yeah.

181
00:14:42,370 --> 00:14:47,450
So when are we doing this?! We're going to
kill all the rotten nobles, right?

182
00:14:47,450 --> 00:14:49,700
You idiot. Think for a change.

183
00:14:49,700 --> 00:14:54,330
But Tamm is right. If we're
going to do it, we're always ready!

184
00:14:54,330 --> 00:14:57,080
--Yeah!
--Yeah, give us the order, Riheet!

185
00:14:57,080 --> 00:14:59,120
We'll do it! Bring it on!

186
00:14:59,120 --> 00:15:00,370
Shut up.

187
00:15:02,790 --> 00:15:05,450
We just took the first step.

188
00:15:05,450 --> 00:15:09,910
Yeah. We don't want to get
ahead of ourselves and mess this up.

189
00:15:09,910 --> 00:15:13,790
We dark elves have been oppressed
by Orvelia for a hundred years.

190
00:15:13,790 --> 00:15:17,250
We've finally been given the
opportunity to take revenge...!

191
00:15:18,620 --> 00:15:20,620
We follow you.

192
00:15:22,160 --> 00:15:27,160
It'll be fun to see the looks on their faces
when we take control of this nation!

193
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:30,620
Until then, we'll pretend to be harmless.

194
00:15:32,370 --> 00:15:33,700
So loud...

195
00:15:39,450 --> 00:15:42,500
This whole nation will be ours.

196
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:33,450
Good, you're keeping up with your training.

197
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:35,000
I'm just following orders.

198
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:39,450
Right, orders. I guess it's been a while
since the scouts took off...

199
00:16:39,450 --> 00:16:41,870
They do seem to be taking
longer than they should.

200
00:16:41,870 --> 00:16:44,660
--Yes...
--I wonder if something went wrong.

201
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:49,040
Clause is with them, I'm sure they're fine.

202
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:53,250
I don't see any Demons anywhere.

203
00:16:53,250 --> 00:16:57,410
Are we sure those sightings are accurate?

204
00:16:57,410 --> 00:17:02,330
Who knows? It's possible they saw wolves
or something and mistook them as Demons.

205
00:17:02,330 --> 00:17:08,040
That sounds likely. I want to head back
and get something nice to eat...

206
00:17:09,830 --> 00:17:11,870
What's wrong, Clause?

207
00:17:11,870 --> 00:17:13,290
There's something out there.

208
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:16,330
Prepare for combat.

209
00:17:21,120 --> 00:17:22,620
Let's get out of the forest.

210
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:23,870
U-Understood!

211
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:32,660
Are these the Demons?!

212
00:17:32,660 --> 00:17:33,620
Flegg!

213
00:17:33,620 --> 00:17:34,830
I'm fine!

214
00:17:35,910 --> 00:17:37,540
Thanks.

215
00:17:37,540 --> 00:17:38,870
More coming!

216
00:17:40,080 --> 00:17:41,120
Gran!

217
00:17:43,370 --> 00:17:44,410
Stay there!

218
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:50,330
Flegg!

219
00:17:54,660 --> 00:17:57,080
Gran, can you move?!

220
00:17:57,080 --> 00:17:59,120
Flegg, he's...

221
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:02,660
I'll hold them here!
You go to the castle and report!

222
00:18:02,660 --> 00:18:04,950
Dammit... Dammit!

223
00:18:06,330 --> 00:18:07,330
Go!

224
00:18:10,410 --> 00:18:11,580
I'm counting on you.

225
00:18:25,950 --> 00:18:27,450
Nobody gets through me!

226
00:18:29,450 --> 00:18:31,000
I-It's terrible!

227
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,120
What is it?

228
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:34,040
The scouts are back!

229
00:18:34,040 --> 00:18:35,540
But there's only one of them!

230
00:18:35,540 --> 00:18:36,700
Just one?! Why?!

231
00:18:36,700 --> 00:18:37,750
I don't know!

232
00:18:38,950 --> 00:18:40,330
Hey! Kasel!

233
00:18:43,700 --> 00:18:45,370
What happened...?

234
00:18:45,370 --> 00:18:47,330
Did the Demons get them...?

235
00:18:57,540 --> 00:19:00,250
I-I'm here to report...

236
00:19:00,250 --> 00:19:06,950
We encountered Demons in the King's Forest.
Scouts have engaged this threat!

237
00:19:08,330 --> 00:19:10,700
How many Demons were there?

238
00:19:11,950 --> 00:19:14,540
The total number is... unknown...

239
00:19:14,540 --> 00:19:17,370
Hey! Wake up!

240
00:19:17,370 --> 00:19:18,830
Give him medical attention, immediately.

241
00:19:18,830 --> 00:19:21,830
--Yes, sir!
--We must do something...

242
00:19:21,830 --> 00:19:25,660
...or else Demons will enter the capital soon.

243
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:28,370
We must hold off the Demons,
no matter the cost!

244
00:19:28,370 --> 00:19:31,870
Let us send more men into
the forest to defeat the Demons!

245
00:19:31,870 --> 00:19:36,950
More soldiers would just lead to more deaths.

246
00:19:36,950 --> 00:19:39,790
Besides, now is the time
to conserve our power.

247
00:19:39,790 --> 00:19:45,120
There's a chance we could see a flood
of Demons like 100 years ago.

248
00:19:45,120 --> 00:19:47,250
Then what do you suggest we do...?

249
00:19:47,250 --> 00:19:51,750
Use the manpower I have acquired.
The Black Edge.

250
00:19:51,750 --> 00:19:54,870
We cannot trust the dark elves!

251
00:19:54,870 --> 00:20:00,200
E-Exactly! On our honor,
we cannot accept their aid!

252
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:02,580
Do not lose sight of what our enemy is.

253
00:20:02,580 --> 00:20:06,750
Our enemies are the Demons.
When our nation is under this grave threat,

254
00:20:06,750 --> 00:20:11,000
we cannot waste time bickering
over differences in race.

255
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:13,950
Please decide, Chancellor.

256
00:20:16,040 --> 00:20:19,410
Only Gran returned...

257
00:20:19,410 --> 00:20:22,040
So... that's what that means.

258
00:20:25,620 --> 00:20:29,290
I understand how you feel...
but you have to let it go.

259
00:20:37,450 --> 00:20:38,450
Kasel.

260
00:20:40,330 --> 00:20:43,950
Frey, what are you doing here?

261
00:20:43,950 --> 00:20:46,830
I heard the scouts returned, and...

262
00:20:46,830 --> 00:20:49,540
...that only one of them returned...

263
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:52,870
Only Gran came back.

264
00:20:52,870 --> 00:20:55,040
Clause is safe, right?

265
00:20:55,040 --> 00:20:57,580
I'm sure he is.

266
00:20:57,580 --> 00:20:59,790
That's why I have to go.

267
00:20:59,790 --> 00:21:02,200
Go? Go where?

268
00:21:03,580 --> 00:21:05,950
To find Clause.

269
00:21:05,950 --> 00:21:10,290
That's absurd! Kasel, you're just an apprentice!

270
00:21:10,290 --> 00:21:12,870
If you go all alone, and the Demons attack...

271
00:21:12,870 --> 00:21:15,660
I'm still going! I have to save Clause!

272
00:21:15,660 --> 00:21:17,120
Kasel!

273
00:21:17,120 --> 00:21:20,290
I never want to lose anyone again!

274
00:21:20,290 --> 00:21:26,120
I don't want to let anyone else
I care about die! Never again!

275
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:27,500
Kasel...

276
00:21:29,250 --> 00:21:30,870
I'm going with you.

277
00:21:30,870 --> 00:21:33,200
--No!
--Yes.

278
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:36,830
I also don't want to lose anyone dear to me.

279
00:21:36,830 --> 00:21:40,620
Besides, my skills as
a priestess should be useful.

280
00:21:40,620 --> 00:21:42,830
Frey, you need to wait here!

281
00:21:43,750 --> 00:21:47,250
Clause asked me to take care of you.

282
00:21:47,250 --> 00:21:49,790
There is nothing you can say to stop me.

283
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:49,040
In order to protect those dear to us,

284
00:23:49,040 --> 00:23:51,160
we took off on a journey and left Orvelia.

285
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:56,250
At our destination, the King's Forest,

286
00:23:56,250 --> 00:23:57,910
we witnessed a sad reality,
and a surprising truth...

287
00:23:57,910 --> 00:24:00,750
"The Truth, Revealed"
we witnessed a sad reality,
and a surprising truth...

